              "question": "<p>Corticosteroids (glucocorticoids) are ‘steroidal’ anti-inflammatory agents. They are some of the strongest anti-inflammatory medications and as such are used in the case of extreme potential inflammation including in life threatening asthma, autoimmune disorders, post organ transplantation and others. They are much different from the anabolic steroids like testosterone. The corticosteroids are actually catabolic, meaning that they break down tissue. They are also much different from the non-steroidal anti-inflammatory agents NSAIDs like aspirin and ibuprofen. Example(s) of corticosteroids that have anti-inflammatory actions by decreasing all arms of the immune system include:</p>\n"
            },
